\newlabel{tbl:actinf_symbols}{{2}{7}{The Active Inference symbols a GNN specification carries, each bound to the equation of sec.~3 that fixes its role. Read \protect \texttt {A}--\protect \texttt {E} as the generative-model tensors (likelihood, controlled transitions, log-preferences, prior over initial states, habit prior), \protect \texttt {s}, \protect \texttt {o}, \protect \texttt {\texorpdfstring {\ensuremath {\pi }}{pi}}, and \protect \texttt {u} as the inference variables, and \protect \texttt {F} and \protect \texttt {G} as the two free-energy functionals minimized at eq.~6 and eq.~7. Use the table as a decoding key when reading a \protect \texttt {StateSpaceBlock}: every declared matrix name should map to exactly one row here, and the \protect \breaktt {\#\#\ ActInfOntologyAnnotation} bindings described below are what make that mapping machine-checkable downstream}{tbl:actinf_symbols}{}}
\@writefile{snm}{\beamer@slide {tbl:actinf_symbols}{7}}
